extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 26: Dinosaur Swamp printed 57-59 (cache p058-p060, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the OCR and checked line by line against renders of printed 57 and 58. The OCR sets the O.C.C. skill list of printed 57 beside the heading and lore of the left column; the render separates them. Heading and lore on printed 57, the stat block on 57-58, the five special skills on 58, the equipment, Ghillie Suit, weapons, money and cybernetics on 59. || GROUP: under the section heading New O.C.C.s (printed 47), whose introduction calls the classes variations on the Wilderness Scout; the entry states no S.D.C. base, only +4D6+10 to physical S.D.C., so men_of_arms is false and occ_group is optional, matching the held Wilderness Scout. || XP: the Dinosaur Hunter and Pathfinder column (the third) of the Experience Point Tables, printed 74 (cache p075), read off a 300 dpi render; every low bound is the previous high plus one. || BONUSES: printed as Special Bonus. +4D6+10 S.D.C., +1D4 P.E., +1 to save vs poisons and disease (toxins_poisons 1, disease 1), and +1 vs Horror Factor at levels 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13 and 15: horror_factor 1 flat plus seven at_level entries. || SKILLS: each base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Lore: Dinosaurs, Lore: Swamp & Everglades, Track Dinosaurs and Stalking are this book''s special skills, shipped in ~246. The five Special Dinosaur Hunter O.C.C. Skills (printed 58) are granted whole: Stalking and Sign Language are not in the printed list but are numbered among the class''s own skills, and Track Dinosaurs takes the +30% the list prints beside Track Animals. Stalking has no percentage; its situational bonuses are prose in the grant''s note, not bonuses:, because they apply only while stalking. SIGN LANGUAGE: the held Communications row at 25% +5%; this class''s own figure is 35% +4% (printed 58), so the grant is base 35 at 4 per level. Cooking is Cook; Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals; Speak Native Language at 95% is Language: Native Tongue. The non-lethal hunter''s Photography and T.V./Video in place of two W.P.s is in the W.P. note, not a variant. || RELATED: count 7 with floors of two Physical and two across W.P. and Wilderness; the schedule is two each at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Horsemanship prints +10% beside General only, Medical +10% beside First Aid and +5% beside Holistic Medicine, Science +5% beside the two Mathematics, so each is split into entries. Technical is any (+5%) except Cyberjacking with +10% to Falconry, Lore and Language: Lore and Language are a +10% entry by prefix; Falconry is filed under Military, which the class takes at +10% already. Field Armorer is Field Armorer & Munitions Expert, filed under Military. Exotic Animals and Holistic Medicine counting as two selections is in the note, not enforced. || HAND TO HAND: Expert; Martial Arts (or Assassin if evil) costs one related skill. || MONEY: 2D4x1000 credits; the pelts, hides and other goods are a restriction line. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: a hunter''s vest, a wide-brimmed hat or baseball cap, a pair of moccasins, 1D4 pieces of white chalk, a shoulder satchel, 1D4 waterproof sacks, a 20-foot spool of wire, a folding utility knife, 1D6 chemical lights, multi-optics goggles, a few personal items, and the weapons (one per W.P. with 1D6+2 E-Clips or 200 rounds each). They are in GM Notes."
