# Dinosaur Hunter

## Lore

Dinosaur Hunters are the big-game hunters of the swamplands: specialists in tracking, stalking and killing dinosaurs and other large, dangerous animals. Some see themselves as the ultimate predators, others as heroes, daredevils or lords of the wilderness, and all of them are thrill-seekers. In their own domain they move with no wasted motion or sound, and in the swamplands they gain +10% to Prowl, Land Navigation and Detect Concealment.

Many are proud and arrogant. The worst are bullies who refuse to kill a man-eating carnasaur until a frightened village pays their price, in credits, valuables, power or service, and some also take bounties on fugitives, regarding intelligent prey as the ultimate test. Others are brave and generous, giving much of the meat and hides of their kills to local people and hunting predators, monsters and raiders that threaten the innocent.

A newer breed takes no lives at all: devoted to the stalk, they shoot their quarry with a camera, and are becoming valued as reconnaissance scouts, intelligence gatherers and research assistants.

## GM Notes

Lore: Dinosaurs covers living dinosaurs in general and the creatures of Dinosaur Swamp in particular: habits, species, diet, range, defences, the value of meat, hide, teeth, claws and bones, strengths and weaknesses, and identification by tracks and dung. The Dinosaur Hunter knows more about living dinosaurs than the Swamp Stomper does.

Lore: Swamp & Everglades covers the swamplands'' ecology, hazards, wildlife and waterways, and the best ways and paths through them.

Track Dinosaurs is part of the Track Animals skill for this class, and serves as well for avoiding dinosaurs as for finding them.

Stalking is the companion skill to Hunting, though neither requires the other: patiently moving into position for the best shot, or close enough to lunge, grab or grapple, without the animal scenting, hearing or seeing the hunter. Any character who can take Wilderness skills may buy it at the cost of three O.C.C. Related selections; it cannot be a secondary skill.

Sign Language: the Dinosaur Hunters'' own silent language, grown from military hand signals into a full syntax and vocabulary that outsiders cannot follow. Hunters teach it only to apprentices and trusted companions. With the G.M.''s approval it may be bought as a Communications skill or given as an O.C.C. skill to other Wilderness Scouts, Rangers and Special Forces characters, counting as two selections; never as a secondary skill.

The Ghillie Suit is the most important item a Dinosaur Hunter owns after his weapons. Its bonus applies only after a successful Prowl, Camouflage or Blend roll, and it does not hide the wearer from thermal imaging, magic or psionics.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: a hunter''s vest, a wide-brimmed hat or baseball cap, a pair of moccasins, 1D4 pieces of white chalk, a shoulder satchel, 1D4 waterproof sacks, a 20-foot (6.1 m) spool of wire, a folding utility knife, 1D6 pencil-sized chemical lights, multi-optics goggles and a few personal items.

Weapons: one for each W.P. with 1D6+2 E-Clips (or 200 rounds) each, and a Vibro-Knife. They prefer precise long-range weapons such as the JA-11 Juicer Assassin Energy Rifle and Viggo''s custom rifles. A hunter who photographs rather than kills replaces two weapons with a digital camera holding up to 600 photographs and a palm-sized video camera with 48 hours of disks.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dinosaur-hunter');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'dinosaur-hunter';

